Adwait Mane: Okay.

728
01:43:22.160 --> 01:43:28.159
Adwait Mane: So, when the distribution is centered at zero, you can still have force being generated.

729
01:43:28.470 --> 01:43:29.220
Hansol Ryu: Right.

730
01:43:29.220 --> 01:43:37.710
Adwait Mane: But what does that mean for, say, the shortening of the entire… Fiber.

731
01:43:38.020 --> 01:43:42.430
Adwait Mane: Does it… Like, to me, it seems like if…

732
01:43:42.840 --> 01:43:46.500
Adwait Mane: If it's centered at zero, the fiber's not going to shorten.

733
01:43:46.800 --> 01:43:48.010
Adwait Mane: Is that correct?

734
01:43:48.290 --> 01:43:51.209
Adwait Mane: It'll just be at its equilibrium length.

735
01:43:52.600 --> 01:44:02.990
Hansol Ryu: So there are actually two types of forces going on here. One is the spleen-like force,

736
01:44:03.580 --> 01:44:13.189
Hansol Ryu: So… and another one is the closed bridge cycling force. So, closed switch goes through the power cycle, like this.

737
01:44:13.290 --> 01:44:16.719
Hansol Ryu: So it actually actively pulls the filament.

738
01:44:17.540 --> 01:44:26.699
Hansol Ryu: So you will still get that force even if your forces are centered along zero. So, even if your displacements are centered along zero.

739
01:44:29.140 --> 01:44:29.640
Adwait Mane: Oh, great.

740
01:44:29.640 --> 01:44:38.210
Hansol Ryu: Right, that, yeah, if we only look at the spring, like, force, maybe when it is real asymmetric.

741
01:44:38.490 --> 01:44:41.380
Hansol Ryu: I think you can net zero first.

742
01:44:43.370 --> 01:44:48.250
Adwait Mane: Well, I understand that you can generate force, but.

743
01:44:48.650 --> 01:44:52.870
Adwait Mane: Will it shorten if it is centered at zero? Will the fiber shorten?

744
01:44:53.400 --> 01:44:56.599
Hansol Ryu: When the fiber shortens, do you still…

745
01:44:56.600 --> 01:45:03.670
Adwait Mane: It seems like if you want the fiber to shorten, the distribution has to be left-shifted.

746
01:45:04.020 --> 01:45:07.130
Hansol Ryu: Yeah, it will get shifted to the left a little bit, yeah.

747
01:45:07.130 --> 01:45:08.840
Adwait Mane: Okay. Okay.

748
01:45:09.400 --> 01:45:13.930
Hansol Ryu: But yeah, when it goes too far away, detachment rate increases.

749
01:45:13.930 --> 01:45:14.330
Adwait Mane: Okay.

750
01:45:14.330 --> 01:45:18.970
Hansol Ryu: We will start losing it, and then they will populate again near the center.

751
01:45:19.510 --> 01:45:20.620
Adwait Mane: Oh, okay.

752
01:45:20.750 --> 01:45:22.819
Adwait Mane: Oh, okay, interesting, as well.

753
01:45:23.800 --> 01:45:27.519
Adwait Mane: Like, feedback, sort of, going on.

754
01:45:27.720 --> 01:45:29.050
Hansol Ryu: Right, right, yeah.

